    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67222" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετοχλίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>remove by a lever, hoist</i> a heavy body <i>out of the
				way</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ κέν τις . . , οὐδὲ μάλ᾽ ἡβῶν,
					ῥεῖα μετοχλίσσειεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.188
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ κ᾽ ὀχῆα ῥεῖα μετοχλίσσειε
				θυράων</span>
			<i>would</i> he easily <i>push back</i> the bolt of the doors,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.567
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				627
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.81
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γῆ -ίζουσα [τὸν
			Ἀνταῖον</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.21
			</span></i>.</div>
